gguf-rco step 6g: a mixed-type merged layer keeps its shards as their own
contiguous tensors instead of views of a zero-padded concatenation (the
compiled graph materialised every strided view before the custom op: 37
copies of about 45 MB per decode step, 2.4 ms; the prefill path copied each
shard per call). Same-type merged layers keep the one concatenated tensor and
the single call. Applies after 0022, 0023, 0024 and 0027.

